                             multiply a number by a variable, we               
                             write them together without the                   
                             multiplication symbol. For example,               
                             instead of writing 5 times x, we simply           
                             write 5x. The number in front is called           
                             the coefficient, and the letter is the            
                             variable. So in 5x, 5 is the                      
                             coefficient, and x is the variable.               
