[06/05/26 17:12:17] INFO     Transcription:  This works because in   base.py:98
                             algebra, when a number and letters sit            
                             side by side with no symbol between               
                             them, it always means multiplication,             
                             never addition, subtraction, or                   
                             division. We always write the number              
                             first, then the variable. So 5x can               
                             only mean 5 times x. This rule is                 
                             universal. Mathematicians everywhere              
                             follow it. So 5x means exactly the same           
                             thing in every country and every                  
                             textbook. By omitting the                         
                             multiplication symbol, we avoid clutter           
                             and create expressions that are faster            
                             to read and write, while keeping the              
                             meaning crystal clear.                            
