[06/05/26 17:12:47] INFO     Transcription:  Now, let us use this    base.py:98
                             idea to describe patterns. Imagine a              
                             sequence where the first term is 3, the           
                             second is 6, the third is 9, and so on.           
                             Each term is 3 times its position. If             
                             we call the position n, then the                  
                             general term is 3n. When n equals 1, we           
                             get 3. When n equals 2, we get 6. This            
                             formula, 3n, captures the entire                  
                             pattern concisely.                                
